 ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml b/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml
index ae6b82b6b2..bf34a252d1 100644
--- a/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml
+++ b/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml
@@ -123,10 +123,12 @@ games:
   - game: tn36
     reproducibility: unsolved
     levels_reproduced: 0
-    win_condition: "unknown; explorer ERRORED before advancing (still errors under E1 salience ordering)."
+    win_condition: "MATCH a movable object to a target on FIVE attributes simultaneously: x, y, scale, rotation, and sjmtdfxdrc (a 5th property). Source: tn36.py:2153 vklyonlcrw = (obj.x==tgt.x and obj.y==tgt.y and obj.scale==tgt.scale and obj.rotation==tgt.rotation and obj.sjmtdfxdrc==tgt.sjmtdfxdrc). L1 at reset: obj=(x30,y13,s1,r0,sj11) tgt=(x30,y33,s1,r0,sj11) -> ONLY y is wrong (move down 20). Internal state is readable: env._game.fdksqlmpki.bzirenxmrg.{htntnzkbzu(obj),aqszntqeae(tgt)}."
+    action_model: "ACTION6 click; data schema IS {x,y} and display->grid is 1:1 (camera.display_to_grid(30,13)==(30,13)). Clicks register (121/121 change the grid). Control is a PROGRAM/transform EDITOR, not direct steering: dispatch (tn36.py:2500) routes a click to a tool-palette (miytdaqzei, EMPTY at reset) else mvqheosngn(apply/2nd-object) else bzirenxmrg(the object); the object carries a move-program vkuvtkaerv=[3,0,3,0,0]; clicking it runs mmmdksslmq()->olrpupaury(). The exact EDIT->EXECUTE semantics that drive obj.y 13->33 are not yet cracked (directly invoking mmmdksslmq did NOT move the object; palette empty)."
     gotchas:
-      - "DEAD-END (2026-06-17 sweep, confirmed again post-E1): ACTION6 raises KeyError 'x' in the game's perform_action — tn36's click payload schema is NOT {x,y}. rich_action_candidates emits {x,y} clicks that tn36 rejects. This is tn36's per-game DELTA: reverse-engineer its ACTION6 data format. Keyboard-only explore also no-advanced (it IS a click game)."
-    next: "RE tn36's ACTION6 data schema; wrap clicks in the game's expected payload before the explorer can advance it."
+      - "CORRECTION (2026-06-17, deep RE): the prior 'ACTION6 schema is NOT {x,y} / KeyError x / explorer ERRORED' note is STALE/WRONG. {x,y} works; the KeyError only fires for data=None. rich_action_candidates emits {x,y} and graph_explore_solve_v2 runs CLEAN on tn36 (no error) — it just NO-ADVANCEs because the win needs the program-editor mechanic, not blind clicks."
+      - "tn36 is a multi-attribute alignment puzzle (move+scale+rotate+property to match a target), far harder than lp85's +1,+1 position-match — blind graph-explore can't drive 5 attributes onto a target."
+    next: "Crack the program-editor control: how is the object's vkuvtkaerv move-sequence EDITED (the palette miytdaqzei is empty at reset — find what populates it) and EXECUTED so obj.y goes 13->33. CLUE: the object's real clickable sub-button is sxhtkytekm, a 9x9 target at grid (32,51) [center ~(36,55)] — clicking the object's BOX is a no-op; this button (object.rawolunrbj only returns True when sxhtkytekm is hit) is the control. Executing the move-program via mmmdksslmq/ujhjvxuwae did NOT move the object, so [3,0,3,0,0] is not a direct move-sequence. Then build an adapter with hand_verifier=vklyonlcrw + goal_distance=sum of the 5 attribute mismatches (read from internal state), state_key=(x,y,scale,rotation,sjmtdfxdrc)."
 
